 "created_at": "2025-05-05T14:18:42Z", "repo": "harm", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "925bfeccb104ee76665e5c0e83712afb79fc6d77", "message": "Changed the behaviour of the contingency matrix: now AFCT is calculated by using the truth value of the consequent whose evaluation starts at 'the current evaluation unit' + 'maximum temporal length of the antecedent' when using |-> or |=>, even if the antecedent fails before its max temporal length.", "created_at": "2025-04-24T10:43:12Z", "repo": "harm", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "849d44a9fb5c6282a3d8eec3539a50f6ebfae70a", "message": "Changed the behaviour of the contingency matrix: now the |=> operator will shift forward by one instant only if the antecedent is true. This effectively makes expressions like 'G(var ##1 true |-> con)' and 'G(var |=> con)' produce the same contingency table for AFCT and AFCF.", "created_at": "2025-04-10T14:50:05Z", "repo": "harm", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "67ec19e7b5e4ca5f4e462605a0613592bb3d46e6", "message": "It now mandatory to add the K or K+ option in the numeric tag", "created_at": "2025-04-03T13:29:02Z", "repo": "harm", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "0b50fa58813ce909af05e15cb692aac7d1f6e975", "message": "updated Dockerfile", "created_at": "2025-03-25T13:28:45Z", "repo": "harm", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3d15103e60a8d47861b822f517badb0dca8260d6", "message": "fixed find boost for Ubuntu20.04", "created_at": "2025-03-25T13:22:26Z", "repo": "harm", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e42059320a829997d0f113c134b373ae9b425fd6", "message": "Added more explainations on the use of --vcd-r and --vcd-ss", "created_at": "2025-03-19T17:51:10Z", "repo": "harm", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_i